---
description: Replay a disrupted performance from its approved checkpoint while preserving only observed execution.
args: { production: ImmersiveProduction; checkpoint: TheatreCheckpoint; incident: ShowIncident; dramaturgy: DramaturgyMap; cues: CueSequence; showEvidence: EvidenceItem[] }
returns: ContinuityReplay
---
1. Bind authority = reconcileCheckpointAuthority(production, checkpoint, incident, showEvidence). Preserve its exact unresolved source, run or hold bindings. Bind replay = replayObservedCueReceipts(production, incident, cues, showEvidence, checkpoint), then knowledge = advanceAudienceKnowledgeAtCheckpoint(incident, replay, dramaturgy, checkpoint, showEvidence).
2. Bind blockers to authority.blockers, replay.conflicts and any unresolved knowledge transfer required for the proposed continuation. The safetyHold and holdSignalIds come from authority's current run-bound stop and all-clear evidence. A proposal, generic approval, or a differently scoped all-clear cannot release an active stop.
3. Bind proposedCheckpoint as the complete source checkpoint with priorCheckpointId set to checkpoint.id, a deterministic proposed ID bound to the actual production/version and new observed receipt identities, and state held when safetyHold is true or proposed otherwise. Preserve its original version as the source version until an exact host commit supplies the new version. Set executedCueReceiptIds to replay.actualPath, audienceKnowledgeByGroup to knowledge.byAudienceGroup and characterKnowledgeById to knowledge.byCharacter. Preserve source history and reservations; add only source-established selected-route reservations. Retain unresolved pending cues and remove a pending cue only when its matching actual receipt or authoritative cancellation establishes the transition.
4. Return ContinuityReplay { sourceCheckpoint: checkpoint.id, newCheckpointId: proposedCheckpoint.id, actualPath: replay.actualPath, unobservedPlans: replay.unobservedPlans, knowledgeByAudienceGroup: knowledge.byAudienceGroup, safetyHold: authority.safetyHold, holdSignalIds: authority.holdSignalIds, resetTasks: the incident-specific evidenced post-show reset obligations, blockers, proposedCheckpoint }. Missing reset instructions produce a review question, not a fabricated completed reset.
5. The proposed checkpoint is resumable data for review. Neither its identifier nor an ordinary application commit establishes physical cue execution or clears the independent production safety interlock.
